03T20:05:27+00:00\", \"dateModified\": \"2019-10-17T09:50:15+00:00\", \"lastReviewed\": [\"2019-06-18T00:00:00+00:00\", \"2022-06-18T00:00:00+00:00\"], \"reviewDue\": \"2022-06-18T00:00:00+00:00\", \"keywords\": [\"Osteoporosis\", \"Fractures\"], \"code\": [{\"@type\": \"MedicalCode\", \"codeValue\": \"\", \"codingSystem\": \"SNOMED-CT\"}]}, \"url\": \"https://api.nhs.uk/conditions/osteoporosis/\", \"name\": \"Osteoporosis\"}, {\"description\": \"Read more about ovarian cancer, which is a cancer that begins in the ovaries - 2 small organs that store women\'s eggs\", \"linkRelationship\": \"Result\", \"@type\": \"LinkRole\", \"articleStatus\": \"published\", \"mainEntityOfPage\": {\"@type\": \"MedicalWebPage\", \"genre\": \"condition\", \"datePublished\": \"2017-10-20T14:12:16+00:00\", \"dateModified\": \"2020-09-04T11:26:00+00:00\", \"lastReviewed\": [\"2020-02-10T00:00:00+00:00\", \"2023-02-10T00:00:00+00:00\"], \"reviewDue\": \"2023-02-10T00:00:00+00:00\", \"keywords\": [\"Ovarian cancer\", \"Chemotherapy\", \"Cancer and tumours\", \"Uterine cancer\"], \"code\": [{\"@type\": \"MedicalCode\", \"codeValue\": \"\", \"codingSystem\": \"SNOMED-CT\"}]}, \"url\": \"https://api.nhs.uk/conditions/ovarian-cancer/\", \"name\": \"Ovarian cancer\"}, {\"description\": \"Read about an ovarian cyst, a fluid-filled sac that develops on a woman\'s ovary. They\'re very common and do not usually cause any symptoms\", \"linkRelationship\": \"Result\", \"@type\": \"LinkRole\", \"articleStatus\": \"published\", \"mainEntityOfPage\": {\"@type\": \"MedicalWebPage\", \"genre\": \"condition\", \"datePublished\": \"2017-10-23T14:07:05+00:00\", \"dateModified\": \"2020-08-12T12:28:59+00:00\", \"lastReviewed\": [\"2019-12-10T00:00:00+00:00\", \"2022-12-10T00:00:00+00:00\"], \"reviewDue\": \"2022-12-10T00:00:00+00:00\", \"keywords\": [\"Cysts\", \"Fertility\", \"Ovarian cysts\"], \"code\": [{\"@type\": \"MedicalCode\", \"codeValue\": \"\", \"codingSystem\": \"SNOMED-CT\"}]}, \"url\": \"https://api.nhs.uk/conditions/ovarian-cyst/\", \"name\": \"Ovarian cyst\"}, {\"description\": \"Find out about overactive thyroid (hyperthyroidism), including what the symptoms are, when to see your GP,  how it\'s treated and why it happens.\", \"linkRelationship\": \"Result\", \"@type\": \"LinkRole\", \"articleStatus\": \"published\", \"mainEntityOfPage\": {\"@type\": \"MedicalWebPage\", \"genre\": \"condition\", \"datePublished\": \"2017-10-20T11:10:09+00:00\", \"dateModified\": \"2020-03-04T12:13:04+00:00\", \"lastReviewed\": [\"2019-09-24T00:00:00+00:00\", \"2022-09-24T00:00:00+00:00\"], \"reviewDue\": \"2022-09-24T00:00:00+00:00\", \"keywords\": [\"Exophthalmos\", \"Overactive thyroid\", \"Thyroid hormones\", \"Beta-blockers\", \"Antithyroid drugs\", \"Thyroid abnormalities\", \"Underactive thyroid\"], \"alternateName\": [\"Hyperthyroidism\"], \"code\": [{\"@type\": \"MedicalCode\", \"codeValue\": \"\", \"codingSystem\": \"SNOMED-CT\"}]}, \"url\": \"https://api.nhs.uk/conditions/overactive-thyroid-hyperthyroidism/\", \"name\": \"Overactive thyroid (hyperthyroidism)\"}, {\"description\": \"Read more about oral thrush, which is usually harmless. It\'s common in babies and older people with dentures. It can be easily treated with medicines prescribed by a GP.\", \"linkRelationship\": \"Result\", \"@type\": \"LinkRole\", \"articleStatus\": \"published\", \"mainEntityOfPage\": {\"@type\": \"MedicalWebPage\", \"genre\": \"condition\", \"datePublished\": \"2017-12-21T15:05:38+00:00\", \"dateModified\": \"2020-08-12T12:23:09+00:00\", \"lastReviewed\": [\"2020-07-08T14:47:00+00:00\", \"2023-07-08T14:47:00+00:00\"], \"reviewDue\": \"2023-07-08T14:47:00+00:00\", \"keywords\": [\"Radiotherapy\", \"Chemotherapy\", \"Antibiotics\"], \"alternateName\": [\"Mouth thrush\"], \"code\": [{\"@type\": \"MedicalCode\", \"codeValue\": \"\", \"codingSystem\": \"SNOMED-CT\"}]}, \"url\": \"https://api.nhs.uk/conditions/oral-thrush-mouth-thrush/\", \"name\": \"Oral thrush (mouth thrush)\"}]}'),
